## Phase 3 — Correctness the first release must not ship

Independent of phase 2 and runnable alongside it. All of it must land before
T031, because none of it can be fixed in a published version.

- [x] T012 Deny unauthenticated requests to the demo chat routes. `src/transport/routes/chats.ts:33` — the pass-through fallback becomes a `401` middleware, across all three routes. Signatures unchanged. Correct `specs/hal-engine-chat-routes/spec.md` § When the guard does nothing, which currently states the old default as behaviour. Add a comment to `example/server.ts` noting that its chat route now answers 401.
- [x] T013 Enforce ownership. Export `AuthenticatedRequest` from `src/types/auth.ts`, re-export from `src/index.ts`, restate `HttpAuthMiddleware` in its terms. Replace the four inline casts in `chats.ts` and drop the `?? 'anonymous'` fallback at `:35`. Add a `requireUser` guard answering `401` when `req.user` is absent or its `id` is `undefined`, `null` or `''` — the empty string named explicitly, because `id` is `string | number` and `0` is a legal id. Depends on T012.
- [x] T014 [P] Say what the routes are. A file-head comment in `src/transport/routes/chats.ts` naming the process-local `Map`, stating `_sessionStore` is unused by design, and stating that a REST-created chat id is not a WebSocket session id. Export and parameter both stay. One line per comment — `re-lint/max-comment-lines`.
- [x] T015 [P] Call `onConnect`. Add it to the `deps` object at `src/transport/createServer.ts:50` (its sibling is forwarded on the adjacent line) and to `ConnectionHandlerDeps`; invoke it after the `connected` frame through a deferred continuation, never inline in the `connection` listener — a synchronous throw there corrupts an already-upgraded socket. Widen both hooks to `void | Promise<void>`, route both through one `runHook` helper that logs `{sessionId, error}` and swallows, and fix the four documents that describe the hook, including the example that reads a session field that does not exist.
- [x] T016 [P] Emit structured log lines. `emit` in `src/shared/logger.ts` writes one JSON object per line — `severity`, `message`, ISO `timestamp`, `category`, `data` — with `ERROR` to `console.error` and the rest to `console.log`. Add `src/shared/logger.test.ts` asserting the format contract, and `docs/logging.md` covering the key set, the level mapping, the stream split and the person-identifying fields. No call site changes: all 28 `log.*` calls keep their level, category, message and data.
- [x] T017 **Decision, then change.** `src/transport/ws/validation.ts:31` accepts `send_message` and normalises it away, so the exported union can never contain it; `specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:98,109` documents the alias as supported. An earlier decision said remove it from the code; the spec restructure resolved it the other way. Decide once, then make code, exported types and spec agree. A deprecation window is required if any client is sending the alias. Resolved by removing it: no client sends it, nothing is published yet, and the exported types never admitted it.
- [x] T018 [P] Give a reporter somewhere to go. Add `SECURITY.md` (intake channel, acknowledgement target, supported versions written for a pre-1.0 package with no maintenance branch, coordinated disclosure, and an in-scope list naming at minimum `src/transport/`, `src/orchestration/tools/` and `src/providers/`); a `## Security` section in `README.md` repeating the address verbatim; a `bugs` field in `package.json`; a security contact link in `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/config.yml`. The address must live somewhere that works even if the repository stays private.
</document>
</section>
